# Game backup and live port

- Treat all current files and changes inside this repository as approved game state for backup.
- When the user asks to update Git for backup, stage and commit the complete current repository state unless the user names an exclusion.
- The canonical live-testing URL is `http://127.0.0.1:5196/`. It must serve the current working tree through the Vite development server with HMR and automatic page reload disabled.
- Saved file changes must become visible only after the user manually reloads the page, so an active run is never interrupted by development edits.
- When the user asks to update the build or current game port, do not build, export, freeze, run tests, run asset verification, run acceptance suites, or reload the user's open page. Only ensure the live server is running.
- Create an immutable release or upload archive only when the user explicitly asks for a frozen release, distributable build, or archive.
- Preserve older frozen releases and their files unless the user explicitly asks to replace or remove them.
